{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1147645-are-mage-magic-flashy","id":1147645,"title":"Are Mage magic flashy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-06T19:49:19-07:00","id":1147645,"title":"Are Mage magic flashy?","content":"Can they be flashy? I imagine a mage battle be sort of like a mage from WoW or from DnD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T22:52:19-07:00","id":1147677,"title":"","content":"Not in the mundane world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:07:33-07:00","id":1147681,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you mean by flashy. One of the Akashic could get flashy in the same way that you get a flashy kung fu movie fight would happen and might pass snuff to not get them too horribly beaten down when reality starts paying attention. One of the Sons of Ether could get really flashy by breaking out the &quot;super science,&quot; but is likely to go over really really badly when reality gets down to dealing with its feelings on super science.<br /> <br /> So if we're talking flashy in the mundane reality then flashy would also be a question of how far is the mage willing to push the risk of gaining paradox.<br /> <br /> Then there's just insane gaming of the universe or as a friend of mine phrased it, &quot;f one of them prepared their own universe beforehand they can get really really flashy, If one of them belongs to a religion that thinks getting erased by paradox is a badge of honor it also can get really really flashy. If either one has enough prime to delay paradox for a week or two it's probably also going to be flashy. And if there is a handy chrinos werewolf to auto delerium all the sleepers, it's probably going to be flashy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  Added some stuff. 10-07-2017, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:30:34-07:00","id":1147707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1147645-are-mage-magic-flashy?p=1147681#post1147681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what you mean by flashy. One of the Akashic could get flashy in the same way that you get a flashy kung fu movie fight would happen and might pass snuff to not get them too horribly beaten down when reality starts paying attention. One of the Sons of Ether could get really flashy by breaking out the &quot;super science,&quot; but is likely to go over really really badly when reality gets down to dealing with its feelings on super science.<br /> <br /> So if we're talking flashy in the mundane reality then flashy would also be a question of how far is the mage willing to push the risk of gaining paradox.<br /> <br /> Then there's just insane gaming of the universe or as a friend of mine phrased it, &quot;f one of them prepared their own universe beforehand they can get really really flashy, If one of them belongs to a religion that thinks getting erased by paradox is a badge of honor it also can get really really flashy. If either one has enough prime to delay paradox for a week or two it's probably also going to be flashy. And if there is a handy chrinos werewolf to auto delerium all the sleepers, it's probably going to be flashy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am talking about throwing fireball spells and stuff. In one of the books, I think it was the free council that have a group of people summoning demons for a movie to save money on special effect sand stuff if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:39:47-07:00","id":1147710,"title":"","content":"The Free Council is from Mage: the Awakening from the Chronicles of Darkness. This is the (classic) World of Darkness forum where the assumption is we're talking about Mage: the Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T03:51:14-07:00","id":1147722,"title":"","content":"Although it's basically the same answer in either.<br /> <br /> It can be, but paradox will punch you in the face for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T04:45:52-07:00","id":1147729,"title":"","content":"Except, especially as of Awakening 2e, it's not the same answer. Awakening 2e cares extremely little about being flashy in front of people as it relates to Paradox (it's really more of a moral issue since it drives normal folks insane instead, though that will feedback into Wisdom, and then the severity of Paradox later). Awakening's Paradox system is much more about pushing yourself farther than is safe for your skills, not how normal people perceive and/or interpret your magic.<br /> <br /> So, in Awakening 2e, the idea of conjuring something instead of using SFX on a film to save money is unlikely to impact Paradox and there's little reason to care unless you suck at controlling whatever you summon.<br /> <br /> In Ascension, that's easily a ticket to Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T07:53:33-07:00","id":1147763,"title":"","content":"Obvious casting in front of sleepers still triggers it. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I suppose you could build a dragon and let it loose and it would be a while before dissonance pulled it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T18:00:40-07:00","id":1147898,"title":"","content":"I'll leave Mage: The Awakening to people who understand that game. I don't - and frankly have little desire to - so I can only speak for Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> If we're doing so, this question is...complicated.<br /> <br /> First, let's get out of the way what we mean by &quot;flashy&quot;. One of the differences I stress between &quot;high fantasy&quot; and &quot;urban fantasy&quot; is that in the latter, the visibility of magic is limited entirely to the actual Effect being performed. If a wizard waves a hand and causes a chair to levitate in the air, the only thing you see is the wizard's actions and the chair rising. You don't see glowing runes appear in the air or the chair get wreathed in some colorful aura or cloud of sparkles. These sorts of things were implemented by creators working in visual mediums, as a shorthand to let the audience know, without a doubt, that magic was happening.<br /> <br /> Not only does this not fit so well into the urban fantasy mold MtAs is going for - where magic should be mysterious and in the shadows - it would also does a disservice to the game's purposes in two ways. One, by taking the focus away from the tools and techniques used by different mage groups. And two, by making it impossible for magic to be Coincidental, if the very act of using magic always brings about special effects. If the very premise of MtAs is to work, it should be possible for a mage to set things up in such a way that observers couldn't be sure that magic happened at all.<br /> <br /> That said, my very earlier statements establish that plenty of the Effects that mages can use are, by their nature, inherently fantastic. Or they can be, if taken in a vacuum. Mages can levitate chairs, summon fireballs, rip holes into the spirit world, teleport, turn water into wine, animate statues, sprout wings, shrug off bullets, and stop time. All of these things will appear &quot;flashy&quot; enough, each in their own way, just by happening. If not disguised, that is what we call Vulgar magic. And that brings Paradox down on the mage's head.<br /> <br /> But they CAN be disguised, if the mage is creative enough, picks the right time and place, and does a little set-up and pageantry. Summoning a fireball seems much more plausible if the mage happens to be holding a lighter and a can of hairspray. It IS even possible for a mage to &quot;summon demons to save money on movie special effects&quot;, if the mage makes it look like their summoning WAS special effects. There is a skill in MtAs called Blatancy, that is all about how well a character can make impossible feats seem plausible. So yes, you can summon your demons to make that movie.<br /> <br /> It is not remotely a good idea to do so - because demons - but you could do it.<br /> <br /> Although with the amount of effort involved in dressing up a set such that it could look like a trick, and the amount of Paradox that could be garnered anyway if the mage botches, it makes you wonder if it wouldn't still be easier and cheaper (and safer) to use FX anyway. Not even mentioning how those demons expect to be paid for their appearance, <i>and we all know how that goes</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T12:52:59-07:00","id":1148095,"title":"","content":"There's this rule where if you spend more than 10 points of quintessence on a scene (of 5 on one spell) your magick starts becoming flashy...with sparks, and rips in space/time, or other stuff, that makes all your magick Vulgar. It's not a good thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T01:47:58-07:00","id":1148244,"title":"","content":"I would also argue that high levels of specific Resonances - the levels where even sleepers notice something is off - are a solid foundation for the style of a Mage's flashyness when combined with obvious vulgar magic - where any pretense of coincidence isn't even attempted.<br /> Not only do you have a gauge that tells you 'Alright, your Mage is by now so resonant that things are starting to get flashy at times', but it also delivers the apt verbs to describe the flashyness at the same time.<br /> <br /> It's actually a good way, IMO, to help new players visualize the concept of Resonance. At low levels it is merely a vibe and the fingerprint of the Mage's effects. At high levels combined with blatant vulgar magic, it becomes the signature style of visual effects of the Mage. The same way you immediately recognize the signature work of a specific character's magic or abilities in media like comics or movies, based purely on its visuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-09-2017, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}